# Fail2ban — Ubuntu 24.04 LTS

Target platform: **Ubuntu 24.04 LTS only.**

Mission: PBX server (Asterisk + API on 44300). Jails protect SSH (admin), Asterisk (SIP/registration), repeat offenders, and API probes.

## Installer behaviour

- Symlinks `jail.local` → `/etc/fail2ban/jail.local`
- Symlinks `action.d/shorewall.local` → `/etc/fail2ban/action.d/shorewall.local`
- Symlinks `jail.d/pbx3-api.conf` → `/etc/fail2ban/jail.d/pbx3-api.conf`
- Runs `fail2ban-client reload` when available

## Jails

| Jail | Config file | Purpose |
|------|-------------|---------|
| **sshd** | `jail.local` | SSH brute-force (admin access). 3 failures in 10 min → ban 24 h. |
| **asterisk** | `jail.local` | SIP/PJSIP registration and auth failures. 5 in 10 min → ban 10 min. Uses system filter; `logpath` forces file-based matching (avoids journal mismatch on 24.04). |
| **recidive** | `jail.local` | IPs banned in multiple jails. 3 bans in 24 h → ban 1 week. |
| **nginx-badbots** | `jail.d/pbx3-api.conf` | Bad User-Agents / scanners hitting the API via nginx (`/var/log/nginx/access.log`). 1 match in 24 h → ban 24 h. Requires system filter `nginx-badbots`. |

## Ubuntu 24.04 notes

- Fail2ban 1.0.2-3 can fail under Python 3.12 (`No module named 'asynchat'`). Use fail2ban **1.1.0 or later** (e.g. `apt install --only-upgrade fail2ban` or ensure you have a fixed build).
- Test the Asterisk filter:  
  `fail2ban-regex /var/log/asterisk/messages /etc/fail2ban/filter.d/asterisk.conf`
- Test the API jail:  
  `fail2ban-regex /var/log/nginx/access.log /etc/fail2ban/filter.d/nginx-badbots.conf`
- Upstream Asterisk filter:  
  https://github.com/fail2ban/fail2ban/blob/master/config/filter.d/asterisk.conf

## Shipped files

| File | Purpose |
|------|--------|
| `jail.local` | Jail config (sshd, asterisk, recidive); deployed to /etc/fail2ban/jail.local |
| `jail.d/pbx3-api.conf` | nginx-badbots jail for pbx3api; deployed to /etc/fail2ban/jail.d/pbx3-api.conf |
| `action.d/shorewall.local` | Shorewall action (blocktype=drop); deployed to action.d/shorewall.local |
